which is one of these group chat platforms, and especially in a small company, Slack just becomes a hangout spot. It's kind of like email. In email, it's too easy to generate tasks for large groups of other people. I can fire off an email with 22 dues for other people and it takes me five seconds to generate that email. And then it takes up the day of the other people trying to respond to it. It creates this asymmetric ability to waste other people's time. Over time, email has degenerated into a medium with this very low signal and a lot of noise, aka spam.

